_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_

**Add `mocked` import for type-safe mocking in TypeScript.**

The Vue TypeScript CSF Next block should import and use `mocked()` from 'storybook/test' for type-safe mocking, consistent with the Angular (line 35) and Web Components TypeScript (line 316) blocks.



<details>
<summary>🔧 Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
-import { expect } from 'storybook/test';
+import { expect, mocked } from 'storybook/test';

 import preview from '../.storybook/preview';

 import AuthButton from './AuthButton.vue';

 import { v4 as uuidv4 } from 'uuid';
 import { getUserFromSession } from '../lib/session';

 const meta = preview.meta({
   component: AuthButton,
   // 👇 This will run before each story is rendered
   beforeEach: async () => {
     // 👇 Force known, consistent behavior for mocked modules
-    uuidv4.mockReturnValue('1234-5678-90ab-cdef');
-    getUserFromSession.mockReturnValue({ name: 'John Doe' });
+    mocked(uuidv4).mockReturnValue('1234-5678-90ab-cdef');
+    mocked(getUserFromSession).mockReturnValue({ name: 'John Doe' });
   },
 });
```
</details>

<details>
<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>

```
In `@docs/_snippets/automocked-modules-in-story.md` around lines 437 - 455, Add a
type-safe mock wrapper using mocked() from 'storybook/test' and use those
